WebRad
======

WebRad encodes and decodes radio signals in the browser. Audio, pictures,
files and messages are processed locally in WebAssembly workers.

Build and run
-------------

Use Node.js 22 or newer and an existing Emscripten SDK:

    npm ci --ignore-scripts
    npm run build:engines -- --engine all --emsdk path/to/emsdk
    npm run build
    npm start

Open http://127.0.0.1:8080/. Choose another port with
`npm start -- --port 8081`. Live microphone input requires HTTPS or localhost.
Installation hooks are disabled in .npmrc.

Native compilation produces 17 JavaScript/WebAssembly pairs in build/wasm/.
Generated files are excluded from Git. After compiling the engines, reuse
them for subsequent app builds. Use --engine NAME to rebuild one engine.
Source preparation and build orchestration run in Node. Emscripten still
uses Python internally; activate its SDK or use --python EXECUTABLE to
select that interpreter. The --emsdk option is optional when Emscripten
is already activated. Use --prepare-only to generate native source copies
without invoking the compiler.

Checks
------

    npm test
    npm run test:engines
    npm run verify
    npm run check:source

Run the app build before the tests and deployment verifier.

Deployment
----------

Deploy the contents of build/out/ to a static HTTP(S) host. Set version in
build.config.json and rebuild for each release; the build versions local
asset URLs so browsers fetch updated files.

Sources and notices
-------------------

src/app/ contains the interface; src/runtime/engines/ contains browser
runtime modules. Native sources and adapters are in src/engines/, grouped
by category and engine. Build tools are in scripts/engines/.

SOURCE-VERSIONS records upstream revisions and archive identities.
Individual SOURCE.json files record hashes for imported source subsets.
Original copyright, license and third-party notices are retained in the
sources and licenses/. The deployed licenses.html links to those notices.
